{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 2 on change 2622 (commit 5932f4951b27, same Change-Id I7a56a1db0d0fb899db286e78f4f5268108889ff3).\n\nTwo reasons for the new patchset:\n\n1. Verified -1 on PS1 was BASE DRIFT, not a code fault. CI failed identically on all four matrix legs in <1m at the install step: 'error: Extra `grounding-terraform` is not defined in the optional-dependencies table for nava-rebar'. The branch was cut from 0d01df552, two commits behind origin/main, and c57057f41 ('Enable the grounding-terraform extra') is what adds that extra to pyproject.toml. Not a flaky test and not a recheck candidate -- rebased onto c57057f41 (clean, no conflicts), which is also the sha the plan-review attestation was verified at.\n\n2. The LLM-Review +1 on PS1 carried one advisory: the distinct scratch-unavailable operator message and the scratch_unavailable / scratch_detail coverage fields were never asserted. Fair -- routing deliberately reuses the low-disk gap reason, so the gap reason alone cannot tell an operator 'disk full' from 'volume gone', and those two conditions have different remediations. Added test_the_refusal_says_UNMOUNTED_not_merely_low_disk, which pins the message wording, both coverage fields, and the fact that the free-space floor keeps its own distinct wording. In the same already-declared file, so file_impact is unchanged and the attestation stays valid.\n\nRe-verified after the rebase: make lint exit 0, make typecheck exit 0 (758 files), test_review_bot.py 105 passed / 20 skipped, and the three gates plus both scratch suites 95 passed after git add."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788536749557521001,"uuid":"d6b7a058-c2a4-4291-918b-cb0cada1ab72"}